{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Then King Ahasuerus said, and he said</b> — twice, to indicate that the king was angry immediately, and out of the abundance of his anger he said hastily, \"Who is this?\" — twice, as it says, \"In his anger, who is this? You, say: Who is this? Say quickly.\" [Regarding] תי״ו: נבעת [is from the root] זורש [n. perhaps a mnemonic or root-designation label], and the meaning is like נבהל, by decree, and behold [it is] its time [cf. בעתה]."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:13.235206573Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}